## Solution

**Setup.** Since $AB \parallel CD$ and $Q = AD \cap BC$, triangles $QAB$ and $QDC$ are similar with ratio $AB/CD = 4/10 = 2/5$. Place $Q$ at the origin, with line $QAD$ along the $x$-axis and line $QBC$ at angle $\angle AQD = 45°$:

$$A = (2t,\, 0),\quad D = (5t,\, 0),\quad B = (s\sqrt2,\, s\sqrt2),\quad C = \!\left(\tfrac{5s\sqrt2}{2},\, \tfrac{5s\sqrt2}{2}\right).$$

**Constraint from $AB = 4$.**
$$|AB|^2 = (s\sqrt2 - 2t)^2 + (s\sqrt2)^2 = 4(t^2 - ts\sqrt2 + s^2) = 16,$$
so
$$t^2 + s^2 - ts\sqrt2 = 4. \tag{1}$$

(Note $|CD|^2 = 25(t^2 - ts\sqrt2 + s^2) = 100$ follows automatically, confirming $CD = 10$.)

**Constraint from $AC \perp BD$.** Compute
$$\vec{AC} = \!\left(\tfrac{5s\sqrt2}{2} - 2t,\; \tfrac{5s\sqrt2}{2}\right),\quad \vec{BD} = (5t - s\sqrt2,\; -s\sqrt2).$$

The dot product is
$$\vec{AC}\cdot\vec{BD} = \tfrac{29}{2}\,ts\sqrt2 - 10(t^2+s^2) = 0,$$
so
$$29\,ts\sqrt2 = 20(t^2+s^2). \tag{2}$$

**Solving.** Let $p = t^2+s^2$ and $q = ts$. From (1): $p = 4 + q\sqrt2$. Substituting into (2):
$$29q\sqrt2 = 20(4 + q\sqrt2) = 80 + 20q\sqrt2 \implies 9q\sqrt2 = 80 \implies q = \frac{40\sqrt2}{9}.$$

**Area.** The trapezoid area equals $\text{Area}(\triangle QDC) - \text{Area}(\triangle QAB)$:
$$\text{Area} = \tfrac12(5t)(5s)\sin45° - \tfrac12(2t)(2s)\sin45° = \frac{\sqrt2}{4}(25ts - 4ts) = \frac{21\,ts\sqrt2}{4}.$$

With $ts\sqrt2 = \frac{80}{9}$:
$$\text{Area} = \frac{21}{4}\cdot\frac{80}{9} = \frac{1680}{36} = \frac{140}{3}.$$

Since $\gcd(140, 3) = 1$, we have $a = 140$, $b = 3$, and

$$a + b = \boxed{143}.$$

